I've always assumed that "spe" is short for "special",
i.e., it holds the value of the "special property" for
that kind of object.  Different kinds of objects have
different special properties, particular to the kind
of object they are:  weapons and armor have
enchantment, wands and rings and some tools
have charges, books fade if you've read them
too many times, tins can be spinach or not, etc.
To save (a tiny amount of) space, those special
properties are all stored in this one field.

